CONTENT: Mar 12, 2014 · Release date: Oct. 2, 2023. Python 3.12.0 is the newest major release of the Python programming language, and it contains many new features and optimizations. More flexible f-string parsing, allowing many things previously disallowed (PEP 701). Support for the buffer protocol in Python code (PEP 688). A new debugging/profiling API (PEP 669).
