CONTENT: 1 day ago · Discover what's new in Python 3.12. Complete release history, support lifecycle, release dates, LTS schedule and End of Life (EOL) status. Python is a v... 10 hours ago · Python 3.12 was released on October 2, 2023. For full details, see the changelog. Python 3.12 is a stable release of the Python programming language, with a mix of changes to the language and the standard library. The library changes focus on cleaning up deprecated APIs, usability, and correctness. Oct 2, 2023 · This is the stable release of Python 3.12.0 Python 3.12.0 is the newest major release of the Python programming language, and it contains many new features and optimizations. Apr 9, 2024 · Release date: April 9, 2024. Python 3.12 is the newest major release of the Python programming language, and it contains many new features and optimizations. 3.12.3 is the latest maintenance release, containing more than 300 bugfixes, build improvements and documentation changes since 3.12.2. May 27, 2026 · After two years (18 months for versions before 3.13), only security fixes are accepted and no more binaries are released. New source-only versions can be released as needed. May 24, 2022 · Some time after the release of 3.13.0 final, the tenth and final 3.12 bugfix update was released. After that, it is expected that security updates (source only) will be released until 5 years after the release of 3.12.0 final, so until approximately October 2028. What's new in Python 3.12.0? Python 3.12.0 is the newest major release of the Python programming language, and it contains many new features and optimizations. More flexible f-string parsing, allowing many things previously disallowed (PEP 701). Support for the buffer protocol in Python code (PEP 688). A new debugging/profiling API (PEP 669). What's new in Python 2023? Note: Python 3.12.0 has been superseded by Python 3.12.14. Release date: Oct. 2, 2023 Python 3.12.0 is the newest major release of the Python programming language, and it contains many new features and optimizations. More flexible f-string parsing, allowing many things previously disallowed (PEP 701). When will Python security updates be released? After that, it is expected that security updates (source only) will be released until 5 years after the release of 3.12.0 final, so until approximately October 2028. New features can be found in What’s New In Python 3.12. This document is placed in the public domain or under the CC0-1.0-Universal license, whichever is more permissive. What version of Python has been superseded by Python 3.12.3? Note: Python 3.12.3 has been superseded by Python 3.12.14. Release date: April 9, 2024
